component theta keys (default) meaning source Nenkova+08 clumpy torus <code>fagn</code> (0), <code>agn_tau</code> (10) L_torus / L_bol,* ; torus optical depth, grid 5-150 FSPS <code>agn_dust.f90</code>, <code>$SPS_HOME/dust/Nenkova08_y010_torusg_n10_q2.0.dat</code> Temple+21 accretion disc (Wang+24) <code>fagn_bbb</code> (0) F_nu,disc / F_nu,* at rest 5500 A (dust-free young + old stellar spectrum) <code>ceridwen/agn/data/temple21.txt</code> (Prospector's <code>temple.txt</code>) AGN dust screen <code>dust4</code> (0), <code>dust4_index</code> (-1.0) extra screen on the AGN: <code>exp(-dust4 (lam/5500)^dust4_index)</code> times the galaxy's diffuse curve; <code>AGNConfig(dust4_type=1)</code> Prospector <code>fake_fsps.attenuate</code> AGN narrow lines <code>agn_elum</code> (0), <code>agn_eline_sigma</code> (100) L_Hbeta [L_sun] per formed M_sun; Gaussian width [km/s]; 23 lines with Richardson+14 'a42' ratios by FSPS name Prospector <code>AGNSpecModel</code> <p>L_bol,* is the dust-free stellar luminosity integrated over frequency on the model grid using DL07 trapezoidal weights, per formed mass. AGN components scale with formed mass in the same way as stellar emission.</p> <p><code>AGNConfig</code> has the following fixed options:</p> <ul> <li><code>agn_mode</code> selects the implementation.</li> <li><code>torus</code>, <code>disk</code> and <code>lines</code> enable components. <code>None</code> uses the mode's   default: torus only for <code>fsps</code>, all three for the other modes.</li> <li><code>dust4_type</code> accepts 0 or 1; 2 is unsupported, as in Prospector.</li> <li><code>tau_interp</code> is <code>"linear"</code> for FSPS interpolation. Corrected mode also   accepts <code>"log"</code>.</li> <li><code>agn_energy_balance</code> is available in corrected mode. <code>None</code> enables it   when dust emission is active.</li> <li><code>torus_file</code> specifies a template file.</li> </ul> <p>Sampling amplitudes. <code>fagn</code> and <code>fagn_bbb</code> span several orders of magnitude. Sample their logarithms and transform them:</p> <pre><code>priors = {"log_fagn": Uniform(low=-5.0, high=np.log10(3.0)),       # Prospector: LogUniform(1e-5, 3)
          "agn_tau": LogUniform(mini=5.0, maxi=150.0),
          "log_fagn_bbb": Uniform(low=-5.0, high=2.0),               # LogUniform(1e-5, 100)
          "dust4_index": TopHat(low=-1.8, high=-0.8),
          "agn_elum": Uniform(low=1e-6, high=1e-2),
          "agn_eline_sigma": Uniform(low=50.0, high=500.0)}
transforms = {"fagn": lambda th: 10.0 ** th["log_fagn"],
              "fagn_bbb": lambda th: 10.0 ** th["log_fagn_bbb"]}
free_param_init = {"log_fagn": jnp.array([-1.0]), "log_fagn_bbb": jnp.array([-1.0])}
</code></pre> <p>Add <code>log_fagn</code> and <code>log_fagn_bbb</code> to <code>free_param_init</code> as well as <code>priors</code> and <code>transforms</code>. <code>SedModel</code> rejects priors for names missing from the initial parameters. With <code>add_neb=True</code> and <code>add_dust_emission=True</code>, provide priors or constant transforms for <code>gas_logz</code>, <code>gas_logu</code>, <code>duste_qpah</code>, <code>duste_umin</code>, <code>duste_gamma</code>, <code>tau_pow</code> and <code>alpha_pow</code>. AGN lines also add <code>agn_eline_sigma</code>. Nested sampling requires a prior for every free parameter. Dust emission requires both <code>add_dust=True</code> and <code>add_diffuse_dust=True</code>, which are enabled by default. Run <code>examples/agn_demo.py --fit</code> for a full fit.</p> <p>Photometric constraints. Stellar dust emission and the torus both contribute in the mid-infrared. With energy balance enabled, <code>log_fagn</code> is anti-correlated with diffuse optical depth. Mass is also degenerate with SFH shape.</p> <p>In <code>agn_demo.py --fit</code>, using UV-to-24 µm photometry at S/N 20 on an Apple GPU, the 16–84% intervals for <code>log_fagn</code> and <code>logmass</code> contained the input values. The <code>agn_tau</code> interval, 21–76, was just above its input of 20. With an earlier <code>StudentT(scale=1.0)</code> SFH prior, a mock fit underestimated <code>log_fagn</code> by 0.25 dex and <code>logmass</code> by 0.3 dex on CPU and GPU. Both inputs fell outside the 95% intervals even though the maximum-likelihood sample was near the input. Broadband data weakly constrain <code>log_fagn_bbb</code>. Inspect the corner plot when interpreting photometric AGN fractions.</p>
